1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,250
How can a whole country be completely

2
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:04,075
surrounded by another country?

3
00:00:04,425 --> 00:00:07,606
This is Lesotho. It's an independent kingdom

4
00:00:07,606 --> 00:00:10,425
with its own king, flag and government,

5
00:00:10,425 --> 00:00:13,534
and it sits completely inside South Africa.

6
00:00:13,884 --> 00:00:16,681
Only three countries in the world are

7
00:00:16,681 --> 00:00:19,931
fully surrounded by just one other country:

8
00:00:19,931 --> 00:00:22,954
Vatican City and San Marino, both inside

9
00:00:22,954 --> 00:00:25,751
Italy, and Lesotho. Lesotho is by far

10
00:00:25,751 --> 00:00:28,775
the biggest, about the size of Maryland.

11
00:00:29,125 --> 00:00:31,335
How did it happen? In the eighteen

12
00:00:31,335 --> 00:00:34,326
hundreds, King Moshoeshoe the First united his

13
00:00:34,326 --> 00:00:37,122
people in these mountains and defended them

14
00:00:37,122 --> 00:00:40,178
from invaders. He asked Britain for protection,

15
00:00:40,178 --> 00:00:43,104
so Lesotho became a British territory instead

16
00:00:43,104 --> 00:00:45,445
of being swallowed by its neighbors.

17
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:49,440
In 1966 it became fully independent, but

18
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:52,994
it stayed an island of mountains inside

19
00:00:52,994 --> 00:00:54,179
South Africa.

20
00:00:54,529 --> 00:00:57,566
And those mountains are high. Lesotho's lowest

21
00:00:57,566 --> 00:01:00,339
point is fourteen hundred meters above sea

22
00:01:00,339 --> 00:01:02,649
level, the highest low point of any

23
00:01:02,649 --> 00:01:05,092
country in the world. That's why it's

24
00:01:05,092 --> 00:01:07,073
called the Kingdom in the Sky.

25
00:01:07,423 --> 00:01:09,908
In winter it even snows there, and

26
00:01:09,908 --> 00:01:12,248
Lesotho has a ski resort, one of

27
00:01:12,248 --> 00:01:13,929
the very few in Africa.

28
00:01:14,279 --> 00:01:16,843
Its capital, Maseru, sits right on the

29
00:01:16,843 --> 00:01:19,339
border. Cross a small bridge over the

30
00:01:19,339 --> 00:01:22,173
Caledon River, and you're in South Africa.

31
00:01:22,523 --> 00:01:26,093
Lesotho has something South Africa badly needs:

32
00:01:26,093 --> 00:01:29,132
water. Its mountains feed huge dams, and

33
00:01:29,132 --> 00:01:31,942
a giant tunnel project sends water to

34
00:01:31,942 --> 00:01:33,765
the Johannesburg region.

35
00:01:34,115 --> 00:01:36,639
In many villages, people still travel on

36
00:01:36,639 --> 00:01:39,856
horseback across the mountains, wrapped in colorful

37
00:01:39,856 --> 00:01:42,001
wool blankets that are part of the

38
00:01:42,001 --> 00:01:42,947
national dress.

39
00:01:43,297 --> 00:01:46,355
The Maletsunyane Falls drop about one hundred

40
00:01:46,355 --> 00:01:48,868
ninety meters in a single plunge, one

41
00:01:48,868 --> 00:01:52,129
of the highest single-drop waterfalls in Africa.

42
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:54,293
Would you visit a country you can

43
00:01:54,293 --> 00:01:56,656
only reach through another country? Tell me

44
00:01:56,656 --> 00:01:57,535
in the comments.

